.TH CORR 1 "July 2026" "Corresync" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
corr \- local-first mail and calendar CLI and MCP server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B corr
.RI [ --config " path" ]
.RI [ --version ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B corr
controls explicitly authorized mail and calendar accounts through provider-specific
adapters. Corresync does not accept or persist passwords and does not intercept TLS.
.PP
CLI and MCP calls use the same typed application operations, deterministic
policy checks, content-free audit boundary, and authenticated local session
owner. Consequential external writes require an exact preview followed by a
separate commit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B config
Create, locate, show, read, update, edit, and strictly validate the secret-free
configuration.
.TP
.B account
Discover and manage isolated accounts and their provider routes.
.TP
.B doctor
Diagnose local prerequisites and run explicitly requested provider probes.
.TP
.B auth
Open an interactive provider sign-in, inspect content-free session state, or
close sessions and clear in-memory authorization.
.TP
.B mail
Discover folders; list, search, and read messages; create drafts; send reviewed
new messages, replies, and forwards; retrieve bounded attachments; move,
hard-delete, and set read state.
.TP
.B calendar
List calendar event metadata in a bounded time window, or review and create,
update, or cancel one typed event. A provider may expose a typed Teams join-link
creation capability; this does not enable general Teams access.
.TP
.B agenda
Read a bounded, normalized agenda across isolated accounts with account and
provider provenance and explicit partial failures.
.TP
.B import
Plan and approve a bounded read-only scan of one local export into private
account-local staging, or purge only that staging.
.TP
.B monitor
Inspect or configure account-scoped monitoring. Collection defaults to off and
advances explicitly through local notification, durable queue, and an approved
runner.
.TP
.B events
List, acknowledge, or explicitly purge the durable account-local event queue.
.TP
.B daemon
Start, inspect, or stop the authenticated local session owner.
.TP
.B mcp
Run the local stdio MCP server, register it through supported client CLIs, or
print native client configuration.
.TP
.B update
Check the latest stable public release. Explicitly self-update a direct
installation after signed provenance and platform verification, or print the
owner-specific command for a package-managed installation.
.TP
.B completion
Generate a Bash, Zsh, or Fish completion script, or detect and idempotently
install completion for the current shell.
.TP
.B feedback
Print an allowlisted privacy-preserving local report before an explicitly
selected copy, new-file save, or browser-open action. It never submits an issue.
.TP
.B version
Print build and version information.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
corr --version
corr help auth
corr config init
corr account discover reader@example.com
corr auth login
corr auth status
corr mail list --limit 25
corr mail search --all-accounts --query "subject:review" --limit 25
corr calendar list --start 2026-07-17T00:00:00Z \
  --end 2026-07-18T00:00:00Z
corr agenda list --all-accounts --start 2026-07-17T00:00:00Z \
  --end 2026-07-18T00:00:00Z --time-zone UTC
corr calendar create --subject "Design review" \
  --start 2026-07-20T09:00:00Z --end 2026-07-20T10:00:00Z
# Review the output, then repeat with --approve.
corr calendar update --event-id EVENT --change-key KEY \
  --subject "Updated design review"
corr calendar cancel --event-id EVENT --change-key KEY
# Both commands preview only; repeat with --approve to commit.
corr mcp setup codex
corr mcp setup claude-code
corr mcp setup github-copilot
corr mcp setup gemini-cli
corr mcp setup qwen-code
corr mcp setup qoder
corr import scan ./synthetic-export --approve-read
corr monitor enable --mode notify --notification-field sender --approve
corr monitor status
corr events list
corr feedback --last-error
corr completion install
corr update
corr update check
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
An operation or diagnostic failed.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was invalid.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable terminal color and styling when set to any value.
.TP
.B TERM=dumb
Disable terminal color and styling.
.TP
.B VISUAL
Editor command used by
.BR "corr config edit" .
.TP
.B EDITOR
Fallback editor command used when
.B VISUAL
is unset.
.SH SECURITY
Mail and calendar content is untrusted private input. Review exact previews
before committing a write. Approval tokens are short-lived secret capabilities
and must not be logged or persisted. If a write reports an unknown outcome,
inspect provider state before retrying.
.PP
Import files and event-queue values are also untrusted. Monitoring, runner
execution, content release, and remote egress are separate consent boundaries.
An automatically triggered runner does not gain write authority.
.PP
Only use
.B corr
with accounts and data you are authorized to access. Provider contracts can
change without notice; run an explicit online doctor probe after an update or
unexplained compatibility failure.
.PP
Automatic update checks read only public release metadata, cache results for
24 hours, and never write notices to MCP, completion, daemon, piped, or JSON
output. Only an explicit
.B corr update
may replace a verified direct installation; package-manager files are never
modified. Set CORRESYNC_NO_UPDATE_CHECK=1 or configure disable_automatic_checks
to opt out of startup checks.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I config.toml
The effective path is printed by
.BR "corr config path" .
It contains account routes, browser settings, credential references, monitoring
consent, and policy only; it must not contain passwords, cookies, OAuth grants,
helper results, bearer tokens, or canary values.
.SH SEE ALSO
Command-specific help is available from
.BR "corr command --help"
or
.BR "corr help command" .
Project documentation and the security policy are distributed with release
archives and native packages.
